  "description": "A severe squall line (tops FL450-500) lies NNW-SSE across the western half of the sector, moving east-north-east at about 23 kt, with one gap about 22 NM wide near y = -10. Trailing stratiform rain behind it. Every east-west flight has to get through the gap.",
